<% const pageScripts = ['/js/about.js']; %>
<%- include('partials/header', { pageTitle, theme, lang, direction }) %>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>
<% const metrics = aboutMetrics || {}; %>
<main id="main" class="about-page layout">
  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="about-hero__body">
      <div class="about-hero__heading">
        <h1><%= t.about_heading || 'About the Hope Turtle Project' %></h1>
        <p class="about-hero__subheading"><%= t.about_subheading || '- A human to human intention' %></p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-metrics" aria-label="Hope Turtle platform metrics">
        <article class="metric-card about-metric">
          <span class="metric-label"><%= t.metric_turtles || 'Turtles' %></span>
          <span class="metric-value"><%= Number(metrics.turtles || 0).toLocaleString() %></span>
        </article>
        <article class="metric-card about-metric">
          <span class="metric-label"><%= t.about_metric_users || 'Users' %></span>
          <span class="metric-value"><%= Number(metrics.users || 0).toLocaleString() %></span>
        </article>
        <article class="metric-card about-metric">
          <span class="metric-label"><%= t.about_metric_boats || 'Boats' %></span>
          <span class="metric-value"><%= Number(metrics.boats || 0).toLocaleString() %></span>
        </article>
        <article class="metric-card about-metric">
          <span class="metric-label"><%= t.about_metric_hubs || 'Hubs' %></span>
          <span class="metric-value"><%= Number(metrics.hubs || 0).toLocaleString() %></span>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-hero__media">
      <video
        src="/vids/hope-turtle-floating.mp4"
        class="about-hero__video"
        controls
        autoplay
        muted
        playsinline
        aria-label="Hope Turtle gently floating across the ocean"
      ></video>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="about-content">
    <%#
    <p><%= t.about_paragraph1 %></p>
    <p><%= t.about_paragraph2 %></p>
    <p><%= t.about_paragraph3 %></p>
    <p><%= t.about_paragraph4 %></p>
    <p><%= t.about_paragraph5 %></p>
    %>

    <p>The Hope Turtle Project is a regenerative, open-source humanitarian initiative that designs and deploys small solar-powered marine vessels to deliver aid across open water to people who need it most. Rather than relying on centralised logistics or political permission, the project takes a radically different approach — building a decentralised, community-powered system where anyone, anywhere in the world can take direct, meaningful action to help a fellow human being.</p>

    <p>Each Hope Turtle is a buoyant marine vessel built primarily from bamboo and repurposed bottles — materials that are widely available, inexpensive, and biodegradable. Inspired by ancestral Austronesian seafaring traditions, the design harnesses ocean currents, wind, and solar energy rather than fossil fuels. Version 1.0 is a hand-assembled structure that carries six food-filled bottles as payload. Version 2.0 integrates onboard electronics, GPS navigation, telemetry, and self-steering — enabling independent voyages across hundreds of kilometres of open sea.</p>

    <p>Supporting the physical vessels is the hopeTurtles.org human-to-human platform — a transparent, open-source web application that connects senders and recipients directly. People in need can request specific items; supporters around the world respond by packing a bottle, registering it with a unique serial number, and dispatching it. When a turtle arrives, the recipient can look up their sender and share news of its safe arrival — creating a living record of solidarity and connection.</p>

    <p>The project is grounded in Earthen ecological principles and a commitment to radical transparency and non-violence. All designs, source code, and research are publicly available. The vessels are engineered to be as organic and biodegradable as possible — so that even if a turtle ends its journey unexpectedly, it leaves behind nutrition rather than pollution. This regenerative philosophy extends to the platform, the community, and the culture of the project itself.</p>

    <p>The Hope Turtle Project is not simply a technology project — it is an invitation. An invitation to imagine and embody a world in which compassion travels freely across borders and oceans. By keeping costs low and designs open, the project is built to grow: engineers, makers, sailors, and communities everywhere are invited to build their own Hope Turtles, commission deployments, and join a growing global bale of people committed to turning concern into care. Every turtle in the water is a small, humble, powerful act of hope.</p>

    <div class="about-actions">
      <a
        class="button"
        href="/Hope_Turtle_Whitepaper--June_2026.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <i class="fa-solid fa-file-pdf" aria-hidden="true"></i> Read the White Paper
      </a>
      <a
        class="button ghost"
        href="https://github.com/h2h-project/turtleOS"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <%= t.about_cta_github || 'View the project on GitHub' %>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer', { pageScripts }) %>
